description: MCP server crate that exposes the Sigil compiler and runtime as Model Context Protocol tools for agent-driven workflows
includes:
  - crates/sigil-mcp/
  - Cargo.toml
excludes:
  - crates/sigil-mcp/target/
context: |
  This crate owns the Model Context Protocol (MCP) server that exposes the
  Sigil compiler and runtime as JSON-RPC tools so an LLM agent can drive the
  compile-feedback loop directly. It is the on-ramp for agent harnesses
  (Claude Code, Claude Desktop, the bench harness) into Sigil.

  Architecture: agent-driven loop. This server exposes verification primitives
  but contains no LLM access of its own — the calling harness owns iteration.
  Transport is newline-delimited JSON-RPC 2.0 over stdin/stdout per the MCP
  stdio transport (no LSP-style Content-Length headers).

  Keep this crate thin: it should compose `sigil-compiler` and `sigil-runtime`
  rather than duplicate language semantics or runtime internals. New tools
  belong here if they expose existing compiler/runtime capability over the
  JSON-RPC envelope; they belong in the underlying crate if they add new
  language or runtime behavior.

  Current MCP tools:
  - `sigil_check(source)` — compile-only; returns the diagnostic JSON envelope
  - `sigil_forge(source, fuel, input, grants, ...)` — compile + ephemeral
    Wasmtime execution; returns `output_text`/`output_bytes`/`fuel_consumed`
    on success. Tool modules must export `pub fn tool_main(input_ptr: i64,
    input_len: i64) -> i64`. Network and filesystem access require explicit
    `IoGrants`; without grants, FFI returns 403.
  - `sigil_lookup_error(code)` — registry entry for a diagnostic code
    (`T###`, `R###`, `O###`, etc.) including hint and doc URL
  - `sigil_inspect_uses(source)` — parsed `use` declarations per module;
    used by the bench harness's stdlib-usage check (purely advisory)

  Integration tests under `tests/` spawn the compiled binary and drive it
  over real stdio so the protocol surface is exercised exactly as an agent
  harness sees it. Treat that as the boundary contract.
related:
  - crates/.scope
  - crates/sigil-abi/.scope
  - crates/sigil-compiler/.scope
  - crates/sigil-runtime/.scope
  - crates/sigil-mcp/src/.scope
tags:
  - mcp
  - rust
  - json-rpc
  - agent
  - server
